<article class="env-remark" id="03E0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03E0">Remark <span data-tag="03E0">66.15.4</span>.</a> Lemma <a href="/tag/03DZ" data-tag="03DZ">66.15.3</a> holds for decent algebraic spaces, see Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03IK" data-tag="03IK">68.12.8</a>. In fact a decent algebraic space with one point is a scheme, see Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/047Z" data-tag="047Z">68.14.2</a>. This also holds when $X$ is locally separated, because a locally separated algebraic space is decent, see Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/088J" data-tag="088J">68.15.2</a>. </p>
</article>